{"id": "ft23_memory_ordering_volatile_bug", "expected_regex": "(?i)(?=.*race|visibility)(?=.*volatile|memory|ordering)(?=.*fix|synchronized|volatile).*", "exemplar": "Problem A: Data race on `value`\u2014multiple threads can increment simultaneously, losing updates (non-atomic RMW). Problem B: Memory visibility\u2014without volatile, one thread's write to `value` is not guaranteed visible to other threads (reordering, caching). Fix: Use `volatile int value` and/or synchronize access with locks. AtomicInteger is better: new AtomicInteger(0).", "counter_example": "The code has a problem with the integer type being too small for concurrent updates."}
