{"id": "ft36_boolean_xor_equivalence", "expected_regex": "(?i)(?=.*XOR|exclusive)(?=.*(?:A.*B|differ|one.*true)).*", "exemplar": "Simplified form: A XOR B. Name: Exclusive OR (XOR). Proof: The expression is true when exactly one of A or B is true (not both, not neither). Truth table: (T,F)\u2192T, (F,T)\u2192T, (T,T)\u2192F, (F,F)\u2192F.", "counter_example": "The expression is equivalent to A OR B."}
