{"id": "ft58_xpath_injection_xml_parse", "expected_regex": "(?i)(?=.*vulnerable|yes)(?=.*XPath|injection|quote)(?=.*escape|parameterized).*", "exemplar": "Vulnerability: Yes, XPath injection. Attack: search_term = \"' or '1'='1\" produces //user[name='' or '1'='1'] matching all users. Fix: Use parameterized XPath if available or escape quotes: search_term.replace(\"'\", \"&apos;\").", "counter_example": "XPath doesn't support injection attacks like SQL does."}
